A||||8||Eric||I've been burned in more ways than one!||||8||
Z||000000||Eric||04-30-2000||06:52 PM||||Today was the first Autocross of the year here in Columbus, Ohio.  With the weather being so nice, it was a fantastic day to do some racing.  I had a great time seeing other Fieros and getting to make a fool of myself.  Unlike last year, I wasn't very conservative.  I was sliding and spinning and hitting cones left and right.  Chadman didn't show.  I haven't heard from him in the last week so I guess he wasn't planning on coming.  On the brighter side, there were two other Fieros that showed up.  Both were 86's, one a fastback and the other a coupe.  The coupe really didn't show its age well, but the GT was very nice.  It ran in C street prepared because of some suspension mods and racing tires it wore.  I beat the coupe and I think I may have beaten the GT, it was close.  The man who drove it had done it before, but his daughter (or wife?) couldn't make it hookup as well.  I was able to come up with a time 40.3 seconds which put me in fourth of four cars in C stock (I think I'll run in C street prepared cause these guys are too good), but the time was respectable and definatly something I can improve upon.  Before too long, I'm going to get the bugs out of my suspension, buy some Konis and perhaps lower my 88 (if it can be done).  BTW, I was beaten by two 1st gen. MR2s (beat one of them last year) and a late 80s RX7.  Next week is driver's school, so I'll go to that and see what my major malfunction is.  Ya coming, Chadman?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Eric||04-30-2000||06:54 PM||||Oh yeah, I got sunburned too.||||reg||13
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||04-30-2000||08:41 PM||||As long as you had fun... that's why you are there. Those MR2's can be beat by the mighty Fiero, it's the dang Miata's I have trouble with. Aren't they supposed to be in B Stock?<P>Here are some of my results if you wonder how another Fiero did in autocross. I am listed in C Stock.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.team.net/urscca/results/2000/000416.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.team.net/urscca/results/2000/000416.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shaft||04-30-2000||10:35 PM||||Hey, where in Columbus do you guys autocross? I live in Columbus and even though I think it may be fun to do that sometime.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000004||Shiner||05-01-2000||12:30 AM||||I heard from a local car nut that at the last race he was at, the fastest car in ANY stock class was an '88 GT 5 speed.  I guess it had a DAMN good driver behind the wheel.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||05-01-2000||09:20 AM||||Hey Eric!  Sorry I didn't make it to the autocross - I was in AZ all last week and flew in late Saturday.  I had too much crap to do around the house to make it, so I called and left you a message at the (740) phone number you gave me saying I wouldn't be able to make it.  Again, I'm really sorry.<P>As for the driver's school:  When, where and how much?<P>||||reg||9
Z||000006||Eric||05-01-2000||11:07 PM||||Our message machine is broken or was broken, I see there's a new phone on the wall today so maybe we'll be able to actually retrieve the messages now.  Sorry.  <P>Well anyway, I had a good time, and I think this could be a better year for me.  The car seems to be running well with no sign of trouble (knock on wood).  All the events are held at the Delphi parking lot on the West side of town on Broad St.  Usually they have SCCA signs and or racing bannars all over the place.  The cost is $25 for non members and $20 for members of the SCCA.  If you sign up as a first time member of the SCCA at one of the events you'll get to race for free that day.  They are always on Sunday from 8-10AM for tech and registration to 4 or 5PM.  If you have a helmet (Snell 85 or newer I think) you can use that or they have loaners.  I'll try to find out more about the school this week when I call the head dude and then I'll get back to you guys.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shaft||05-02-2000||05:35 PM||||Thanks for lettin me know where it is. I also talked to a friend of mine and he said that he was there with his go-cart. Sounds fun and I may stop by to watch if not race. ||||reg||14
Z||000008||Greg Piet||05-02-2000||05:56 PM||||Well I just got nailed by some guy geting reclassed with his Miata.   I was 3rd for the season in CS, but the 2000 rules have the 1.6 miatas and below in CS now.  So one guy went down to CS and got all of CS adjusted.  So now im securely in 4th instead of 3rd. GRRRR!<BR>The Miata's are tough little cars, but I know I can beat the 1500 miata that is now in CS.   I am really miffed about that since if I knew that the Miata was in my class I would have pushed a little harder at the last race and beat the miata, since I had first secured before the miata was put in my class.<BR>OK OK OK im done complaining!||||reg||1
